WASHINGTON — The U.S. Small Business Administration (SBA) announced today the opening of a Disaster Loan Outreach Center (DLOC) in Lewis County to assist businesses, private nonprofit (PNP) organizations and residents affected by the 2025 Severe Winter Storms occurring Dec. 5 – 22, 2025.

Beginning Thursday, March 5, SBA customer service representatives will be on hand at the Disaster Loan Outreach Center in Packwood to answer questions and assist with the disaster loan application process. No appointment is necessary, walk-ins are welcome. Those who prefer to schedule an in-person appointment in advance can do so at appointment.sba.gov.

The center’s hours of operation are as follows:

LEWIS COUNTY Disaster Loan Outreach Center Packwood Community Hall 12935 US-12 Packwood, WA 98361

Opens at 12 p.m. Thursday, March 5 Tuesdays - Fridays, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Saturdays, 10:00 a.m. - 2:00 p.m.

The following locations are also open and continue to serve survivors:

